<item>
            <title>[LU-20855] sanity test_65n deletes ROOT default LMV, test_413d fails</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20855</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_65n saves the default LMV of the filesystem root directory by its stripe count, index and hash type, and restores it at exit with a stack_trap.  Since &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13417&quot; title=&quot;DNE3: mkdir() automatically create remote directory on MDS which has more space&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-13417&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-13417&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;mdd: set default LMV on ROOT&quot;), MDT0000 sets a default LMV on ROOT with no hash type:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;lmv_stripe_count: 1 lmv_stripe_offset: -1 lmv_hash_type: none lmv_max_inherit: -1 lmv_max_inherit_rr: 3
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because the hash type is &quot;none&quot;, test_65n takes its &quot;no default LMV&quot; branch and runs &quot;lfs setdirstripe -D -d $MOUNT&quot;, which deletes the ROOT default LMV instead of restoring it.  After test_65n the root directory shows:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;lmv_stripe_count: 0 lmv_stripe_offset: -1 lmv_hash_type: none lmv_max_inherit: -1 lmv_max_inherit_rr: 0
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Later subtests no longer get new directories spread over the MDTs by max-inherit-rr.  sanity test_413d (&quot;inherit ROOT default LMV&quot;) then fails on a DNE system when run after test_65n:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;sanity test_413d: @@@@@@ FAIL: 400 subdirs on MDT0
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is reproducible on a single-node 4-MDT test system with &quot;ONLY=&apos;65n 413d&apos; sanity.sh&quot;; test_413d passes when run on its own.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_65n should check for a default LMV by its stripe count, and restore max-inherit and max-inherit-rr as well, and the hash type only if one is set.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
